   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "672e808e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Setting the teoretical value of d0 (nm) for the desired direction (adjust if you want a different reference)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 59,
   "id": "6624271c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[strain_c] d0 = 0.4130 nm  (~22.57 px), dir = 'za1'\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "d0_nm = 0.413  # in nanometers\n",
    "\n",
    "d0_px = d0_nm / sampling\n",
    "\n",
    "u_c_vec = np.array(za1, dtype=float)\n",
    "u_c = u_c_vec / (np.linalg.norm(u_c_vec) + 1e-12)  # unit vector\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"[strain_c] d0 = {d0_nm:.4f} {units}  (~{d0_px:.2f} px), dir = 'za1'\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a6cf8b46",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Deep dive into the neighborhood and projection part. We chose ckd-tree for efficient neighbor search\n",
    "and za1 (out of plane) as the direction of interest for strain measurement, but you can choose za0 if you prefer (just replace za1 with za0 in the code below)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 60,
   "id": "83076fef",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "pos = np.asarray(subA.atom_positions, dtype=float)   # (N,2) in pixels\n",
    "tree = cKDTree(pos)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6abdf4cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Search for neighbors within a reasonable radius around d0_px; (the bounds help to avoid picking the next/next-next neighbor in the same direction)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 61,
   "id": "9fde7066",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "r_max = 1.6 * d0_px\n",
    "low_bound = 0.5 * d0_px\n",
    "high_bound = 1.5 * d0_px\n",
    "\n",
    "eps_c = np.full(len(pos), np.nan, dtype=float)\n",
    "d_loc = np.full(len(pos), np.nan, dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, p in enumerate(pos):\n",
    "    idxs = tree.query_ball_point(p, r=r_max)\n",
    "    if not idxs or len(idxs) < 2:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    rel = pos[idxs] - p                     \n",
    "    proj = rel @ u_c                        # projection on u_c direction (k,)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # candidates in +u_c and -u_c within the window [0.5 d0, 1.5 d0]\n",
    "    pos_side = proj[(proj > 0) & (proj >= low_bound) & (proj <= high_bound)]\n",
    "    neg_side = -proj[(proj < 0) & (-proj >= low_bound) & (-proj <= high_bound)]\n",
    "\n",
    "    if pos_side.size and neg_side.size:\n",
    "        d_plus = np.min(pos_side)\n",
    "        d_minus = np.min(neg_side)\n",
    "        d_here = 0.5*(d_plus + d_minus)     # symmetric average (more stable)\n",
    "    elif pos_side.size:\n",
    "        d_here = np.min(pos_side)           # fallback (less stable)\n",
    "    elif neg_side.size:\n",
    "        d_here = np.min(neg_side)           # fallback\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    d_loc[i] = d_here\n",
    "    eps_c[i] = (d_here - d0_px) / d0_px\n",
    "\n",
    "edge = 20  # pixels (try 20–60)\n",
    "mask_edge = (\n",
    "    (pos[:,0] > edge) & (pos[:,0] < (img.shape[1]-edge)) &\n",
    "    (pos[:,1] > edge) & (pos[:,1] < (img.shape[0]-edge))\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "vals = eps_c[mask_edge & np.isfinite(eps_c)]\n",
    "p2, p98 = np.percentile(vals, [2, 98])\n",
    "eps_clean = eps_c.copy()\n",
    "eps_clean[~mask_edge] = np.nan\n",
    "eps_clean[(eps_clean < p2) | (eps_clean > p98)] = np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "# symmetric interval (tension/compression) for diverging colormap\n",
    "p1, p99 = np.nanpercentile(eps_clean, [1, 99])\n",
    "vabs = float(np.nanmax(np.abs([p1, p99])))\n",
    "vmin, vmax = -vabs, +vabs\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3eebef2c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Color map and scatter plot to see the strain distribution (scatter on atomic positions, fast, robust). This will generate eaxh unit cell's strain value at the atom positions, and we can visualize it with a scatter plot colored by strain"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 63,
   "id": "f787ee73",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x500 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6,5))\n",
    "\n",
    "sc = ax.scatter(\n",
    "    pos[:, 0], pos[:, 1],\n",
    "    c=eps_clean, s=12, cmap=\"RdBu_r\",\n",
    "    vmin=vmin, vmax=vmax, edgecolors='none'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.invert_yaxis()            # keep y down, like in image coordinates\n",
    "ax.set_aspect('equal')       # keep correct x/y ratio\n",
    "\n",
    "cbar = fig.colorbar(sc, ax=ax, pad=0.02)\n",
    "cbar.set_label(\"Strain ε_c = Δd/d (in c direction)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Strain map (scatter, image convention – y down)\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"x (px)\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"y (px)\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout() \n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
